course: dictionary
lesson: 9761
title: Support: hold up, help, or agree
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Support is a word with several meanings. To find the right one, read the words around it and ask: what would fit here? The meaning changes with the sentence, so the clues matter. «A beam bridge rests on supports» means things that hold the bridge up so it does not fall.
explain: In «Fears usually get smaller when you face them in small, safe steps with support», support means help. Someone is there with you, so the fear feels smaller. Try the meaning in the sentence: "with help" fits, so you know you have it right.
explain: Support can also be a noun, a thing or a feeling. «Support each other» means help each other, and «moral support» means encouragement. A support network is the set of people you can turn to when you need help.
fact: Support as a verb can mean to hold something up, to help someone, to like a team, or to agree with an idea.
fact: Support as a noun means help, or a thing that holds something up.
fact: «Support a team» means like it and want it to win.
fact: «Support your answer with evidence» means back up your answer with facts.
fact: A support network is the people you can turn to, such as family, teachers, the school nurse and helplines.
exercise: «A beam bridge rests on supports.» What are the supports in this sentence? | Songs sung about bridges | Boats that float under it | Paint that makes the bridge bright | *Things that hold the bridge up
exercise: «I support my team, so I cheer loudly at every match.» What does support mean? | To sleep through the match | To hold a team up on their shoulders | To swap teams every week | *To like a team and want it to win
exercise: «Fears usually get smaller when you face them in small, safe steps with support.» What does with support mean here? | *With help from someone | Without anyone knowing | With a heavy bag | With a long stick
test: «Kindness is small and quick online: being an upstander, someone who supports a person being bullied and tells an adult, is not snitching.» What does supports mean here? | Holds up | Ignores | *Helps and stands up for | Likes
test: What is a support network? | A type of sports shoe | A map of the school | A dream about bridges | *The people you can turn to, such as family and teachers
exam: Ben says, «I support your idea, let's try it.» What does support mean? | To lose the idea | To hold the idea up in the air | *To agree with the idea | To write the idea down
